decision: pass
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: What happens when the push gate or locked execution cannot run its checks?

Records the decision that the push gate and lock-based execution fail when a check cannot run (missing engsys, unprepared locked revision or cache) instead of falling back.
Translated from Korean to English as a frozen record; it changes ADR 0013 and complements ADR 0012 as stated in the lead.
Headings mapped to Decision / Context and constraints / Rationale and alternatives / Consequences; the rationale section keeps its test-file evidence and prose alternatives as in the source.
Test paths, ENGSYS_USE_CHECKOUT=1 and command names kept verbatim; no Korean literals retained.
The limitations paragraph (local hook bypass, server checks, dependency state) is kept without change.

